## Lessons Learned

This lab demonstrated how LVM separates physical storage from logical storage. By adding a new Physical Volume to an existing Volume Group, additional storage became available without modifying the original disk. That additional capacity was then allocated to an existing Logical Volume using `lvextend`.

An important part of the process was verifying that the Volume Group contained sufficient free space before attempting to extend the Logical Volume.

