## Real-World Application

Expanding storage with LVM is a common administrative task in enterprise Linux environments. As servers require additional disk capacity, administrators can add new storage devices, extend existing Volume Groups, and increase Logical Volume sizes without rebuilding partitions or reinstalling operating systems.

